- R>W | say out loud, in front of them both, that the old saying was only half true | v: benevolence, universalism | chance: 52
- G>U | take them walking for a week, and let them think it through slowly | v: benevolence, self-direction | chance: 58
works: The young one finds their feet again, and {friend} forgives {N} by the summer.
works: {N} starts telling the whole story, costs and all, and finds it is a better one.
fails: The young one takes {Ns} words as a blessing, and the next leap goes worse.
