== in my day, played back
tier: inner
holds: stuck in their ways
stages: adult, mature, elder
age: 40-110
tone: mixed
life: home, community
horizon: months
roles: friend
earth: a young volunteer records your memories of the town, and played back, every answer is about how much better it used to be
requires: holds the state (force above .5) for six months or more; at most once every three years for this shadow
likelier: a long life in one town; a local history group or library project; much Green in the color history
rarer: a newcomer to the town; a life spent moving
times: Some people who stay in the state, about one in four of them over three years (estimate)
gap: 3-10
scene: A young volunteer records {N} for the town's memory project. Played back at the library, every answer starts with "in my day" and ends with "not any more". The volunteer thanks {N} politely, and looks tired.
scene W: {N} meant to set the record straight for those who come after. On the recording it sounds more like a list of complaints.
scene U: {N} listens closely and hears the same three stories told five ways, and not one question asked back.
scene B: {N} wanted the young to know what {N} had built. What comes out sounds like someone who thinks nothing since was worth building.
scene R: {N} hears {Ns} own voice, sour and slow, and wants to snatch the recording back.
scene G: {N} had thought of it as remembering. Hearing it, {N} wonders whether it was really grieving everything that changed.
- G | let it stand: it was better then, and someone ought to say so | v: tradition | chance: 40
- W | ask to record it again, fairly, with the good that came since | v: universalism, conformity | chance: 62
- U | ask the volunteer what the town is like for them, and listen to every word | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 66
- B | offer to teach your old trade, on your own terms, to people starting out | v: achievement, power | chance: 66
- R | laugh at the old grump on the recording, and tell a story with no complaints | v: hedonism, benevolence | chance: 62
- W>B | join the project's committee, and steer it toward the living town | v: power, universalism | chance: 58
- U>R | learn the new thing in town most grumbled about, and try it once | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: learned a skill | chance: 62
- B>G | pay for the volunteer's next project, on the past and the present together | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 62
- R>W | tell the library meeting, out loud, that the town deserved a fairer hearing | v: universalism, benevolence | chance: 58
- G>U | walk the old streets with the volunteer, and ask what each new place is for | v: universalism, tradition | chance: 52
works: The second recording is played at the library too, and people stop {N} in the street to talk about it.
works: {N} finds that the town, for all its changes, still has room for {N} in it.
fails: {N} agrees to try again, and the second recording sounds just like the first.
fails: The volunteer moves on, and {N} goes back to talking mostly to the radio.
